                        <provenance type="#rejected"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_454">Quarr,
                                Hampshire, Cistercian abbey of St Mary the Virgin</orgName>
                            <p>This attribution was rejected in the second edition of Medieval
                                Libraries of Great Britain (1964), which did not change in the
                                Supplement (1987). The corresponding Medieval Libraries of Great
                                Britain index card highlights a claim by M. R. James: there is an
                                erased monastic mark on the flyleaf; 'the last word is perhaps
                                Quarreria - cf. MS 14'. Ker was skeptical of this, and added the
                                following note on the index card (initialled, and dated 24 April
                                1942): The inscription begins <q>Iste liber constat domino
                                    Rog(?)...</q>. I could not read more, nor 'Quarreria' by u.v.
                                light: M. R. James used a reagent.</p></provenance>
                    </history>
